% An unsafe rule and a cycle through negation are reported in one run.
%
% The rules below are architecture section 9's example as it would be
% written without a positive literal: X occurs only under `not`, so both are
% unsafe, are rejected, and take no part in the dependency analysis.  The
% cycle between even/1 and odd/1 is among the rules that were accepted, and
% is reported alongside them.
a(X) :- not b(X).
b(X) :- not a(X).

num(0).
even(X) :- num(X), not odd(X).
odd(X) :- num(X), not even(X).
